  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PROTECTING THE LOMAMI NATIONAL PARK AND ITS PERIPHERAL FORESTS IN DR CONGO</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO INCREASE THE OPERATIONAL EFFICIENCY OF THE RECENTLY CREATED LOMAMI NATIONAL PARK (LNP), DEMOCRATIC REPUBLIC OF CONGO. THE LNP HARBORS SEVERAL ICONIC ENDEMIC SPECIES INCLUDING BONOBO, OKAPI, AND CONGO PEACOCK AS WELL AS A STABLE POPULATION OF FOREST ELEPHANT. THE PROJECT AIMS TO EXTEND WILDLIFE MANAGEMENT INTO THE CURRENT BUFFER ZONE THROUGH ESTABLISHMENT OF COMMUNITY RESERVES WHILE INCREASING COLLABORATION WITH SURROUNDING COMMUNITIES TO ENSURE BETTER PROTECTION FOR THE PARK AS WELL. ACTIVITIES INCLUDE: (1) IMPROVING MANAGEMENT AND MONITORING SYSTEMS WITHIN LNP (2) SUPPORTING COMMUNITIES IN PARTICIPATORY MAPPING OF AND DEVELOPMENT OF MANAGEMENT PLANS FOR COMMUNITY CONCESSIONS IN THE BUFFER ZONE AND (3) CONDUCTING REGULAR MONITORING AND SURVEYS OF KEY WILDLIFE POPULATIONS AND STATUS OF THREATS.</narrative>
  </description>
